# Sanitization: cleaning user input (XSS prevention)

Package: `Pervaxis.Genesis.Sanitization` (already referenced and registered in this service).

Sanitize every free-text value that comes from a user and is later stored or shown, such as comments, notes, names and descriptions. Do not sanitize IDs, enums or numbers.

## Profiles

| Profile | Result |
|---|---|
| `PlainText` | All HTML removed. This is the default. |
| `SafeHtml` | Safe tags such as bold, italic, links and lists are kept. Scripts, event handlers and iframes are removed. |
| `Markdown` | Everything in `SafeHtml`, plus code blocks, headings, blockquotes, tables and images. |

Custom profiles can be added in configuration (`CustomProfiles`).

## Settings

Read from the `Genesis:Sanitization` configuration section. All values are optional. The defaults are shown.

```json
{
  "Genesis": {
    "Sanitization": {
      "DefaultProfile": "PlainText",
      "AllowCustomProfiles": true,
      "MaxInputLength": 1000000,
      "EnableMiddleware": false
    }
  }
}
```

## Option 1: mark the property on the request model (simplest)

The package runs a filter before validation and cleans every property marked with `[Sanitize]`.

```csharp
using Pervaxis.Genesis.Sanitization.Filters;

namespace {{ model.names.namespace }}.Domains.Comments.Models;

public sealed record CreateCommentRequest
{
    // SafeHtml keeps simple formatting.
    [Sanitize(Profile = "SafeHtml")]
    public required string Body { get; init; }

    // No profile means the default profile (PlainText).
    [Sanitize]
    public required string AuthorName { get; init; }
}
```

Limits of Option 1:
- It only cleans **top-level string properties** of the action's arguments. A string inside a nested object or a list is not touched, even if it has `[Sanitize]`. Option 3 (`Sanitized`) also only works on top-level properties. Use Option 2 for nested values.
- It only runs for values that are not `null`.

## Option 2: call the sanitizer in the service

Use this when the value does not come straight from a request model.

```csharp
using Pervaxis.Genesis.Sanitization.Abstractions;

namespace {{ model.names.namespace }}.Domains.Comments.Services;

public sealed class CommentService(ISanitizer sanitizer, CommentDbContext dbContext) : ICommentService
{
    public async Task CreateAsync(string body, string title, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var safeBody = sanitizer.SanitizeHtml(body);               // keeps safe HTML
        var safeTitle = sanitizer.StripAll(title);                 // plain text only
        var custom = sanitizer.Sanitize(body, "MyCustomProfile");  // named profile

        // ... store the sanitized values
    }
}
```

`ISanitizer` methods: `StripAll`, `SanitizeHtml`, `Sanitize(input, profileName)` and `Sanitize(input, profile)`. All of them return `null` for `null` input.

## Option 3: inside a FluentValidation validator

Two modes: clean the value (`Sanitized`) or reject dirty input (`MustBeSanitized`).

```csharp
using FluentValidation;
using Pervaxis.Genesis.Sanitization.Abstractions;
using Pervaxis.Genesis.Sanitization.Extensions;

namespace {{ model.names.namespace }}.Domains.Comments.Validators;

public sealed class CreateCommentRequestValidator : AbstractValidator<CreateCommentRequest>
{
    public CreateCommentRequestValidator(ISanitizer sanitizer)
    {
        // Clean the value, then validate the cleaned value.
        RuleFor(x => x.Body)
            .Sanitized(sanitizer, "SafeHtml")
            .NotEmpty();

        // Reject the request if the value contains anything that would be removed.
        RuleFor(x => x.AuthorName)
            .MustBeSanitized(sanitizer);
    }
}
```

## Which option to use

- Request models from the API: Option 1.
- Values built or loaded inside a service: Option 2.
- You already have a validator and want the rule next to the others: Option 3.
- Do not apply the same property to more than one option. It is wasted work.

## Not enabled by default

A middleware can clean every POST, PUT and PATCH body automatically (`UseGenesisSanitization()` together with `EnableMiddleware: true`). It is off by default and is **not** added to `Program.cs` in this service. Ask the platform team before turning it on, because it changes every endpoint.
